    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a slate defined by a few high-upside opportunities against soft opposing rotations. The top play of the day is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries a 74.56 efficiency score into his matchup against Burnes. The combination of a favorable 5.41 xERA and a 14% boost from dynamic platoon indicators makes him our premier start, closely followed by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 70.40 score is bolstered by significant park factors that mitigate the danger of facing an elite arm like Misiorowski. **Jackson Merrill** also remains an essential start at 70.07; while his score is tempered slightly by park factors, he is an automatic lock due to his elite stolen base potential, a critical component of our scarcity-driven strategy.\n\nSecondary contributors provide depth, though some caution is warranted against high-end pitching. **Heliot Ramos** (67.50) benefits from the same favorable matchup against Burnes as **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, while **Sam Antonacci** offers a solid 58.70 floor as a leadoff hitter. The toughest decision on the bench was **Josh Jung** (43.41), who was squeezed out of the starting nine. While **Josh Jung** projects as a viable utility piece, his score suffered under the weight of facing a 3.24 xERA arm and a lack of platoon advantage. We are opting to bench him in favor of higher-ceiling plays to preserve our daily cap efficiency.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding risk factors across the board. **Henry Bolte** sits at the bottom of our active projections (41.35) and is only starting due to his leadoff role; facing Williams, G (2.91 xERA) is a clear negative that nearly pushed him to the bench. Additionally, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.39) is entering a difficult battle against deGrom, where his raw power is suppressed by the pitcher\u2019s elite skill set and a 19% penalty to his projection. As we push for late-season Roto gains, the focus remains on leveraging the speed of players like **Jackson Merrill** and the high-volume opportunities of our leadoff hitters to climb the standings.",
